cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this tool, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "IPCC Tier 2 Livestock GHG Uncertainty Calculator"
authors:
  - name: "Alliance of Bioversity International and CIAT (CGIAR)"
    city: "Cali"
    country: "CO"
    website: "https://alliancebioversityciat.org/"
abstract: >
  Free web-based cattle GHG uncertainty calculator for national greenhouse-gas
  inventory compilers: Monte Carlo (IPCC Approach 2) uncertainty analysis of
  IPCC Tier 2 cattle emission estimates (enteric fermentation CH4, manure
  management CH4 and N2O, pasture deposition N2O), with correlated sampling,
  activity-data vs emission-factor decomposition, sensitivity analysis (SRC
  and PRCC), trend uncertainty, and outputs formatted for IPCC 2006 Vol. 1
  Ch. 3 Table 3.3 and UNFCCC Enhanced Transparency Framework reporting.
  Developed by the Alliance of Bioversity International and CIAT under the
  CGIAR Climate Action Programme, funded by the Global Methane Hub
  (grant R-2026-01051).
keywords:
  - GHG inventory
  - IPCC Tier 2
  - Monte Carlo
  - uncertainty analysis
  - livestock
  - cattle
  - enteric fermentation
  - methane
  - nitrous oxide
  - UNFCCC
  - Enhanced Transparency Framework
  - national inventory
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/CGIAR-Climate-Data-Hub/cattle-ghg-uncertainty"
url: "https://cgiar-climate-data-hub.github.io/cattle-ghg-uncertainty/"
